# Architecture: the little-endian Debian release architectures, not "any".
# The binary wire packet is transmitted as an in-memory packed struct with no
# byte-order conversion, and include/types.h + lib/imud_client.h both #error
# on a big-endian host — so "any" promised a build that cannot succeed on
# s390x, ppc64, sparc64 or hppa. Declaring the real set turns that into
# "architecture not supported" at the start instead of a compile error deep
# in the build. Keep this list and those two #error guards in step; adding a
# new little-endian port is a one-line change here.
Package: imud
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, adduser
Recommends: imud-wmm-data
Suggests: imud-utils
Description: IMU daemon — attitude, heading, and heave for boats ("gpsd for IMUs")
 imud reads an I2C IMU and magnetometer, fuses them with a quaternion
 Multiplicative EKF, and serves attitude, heading (magnetic and WMM true),
 rate of turn, heave, and sea-state statistics to the network: NMEA 0183
 over UDP, a high-rate binary UDP stream, and a local AF_UNIX subscription
 socket. A built-in black box can record every raw sensor sample to .imucap
 capture files, and the sim driver replays them (or a synthetic scenario)
 through the full pipeline.
 .
 Includes calibration and self-characterization (imud-cal), a status tool
 (imud-status), the Python client, and a hardened systemd service. The
 network monitor ships as imud-utils; protocol bridges are packaged
 separately: imud-signalk, imud-mqtt, imud-influxdb, imud-mavlink,
 imud-prometheus.
 .
 Requires a little-endian host: the binary wire packet is sent as a packed
 struct with no byte-order conversion.

Package: imud-utils
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: diagnostic tools for the imud IMU daemon
 Operator tools that are not part of the running system.
 .
 imud-mon is a terminal monitor that decodes the daemon's NMEA and binary
 UDP output streams live, from any machine on the network. It is wire-pinned
 to the daemon's packet version: keep imud-utils and imud at the same release.
 .
 imud-imutest validates a sensor driver against real hardware and writes a
 Markdown report suitable for attaching to a bug report. It exercises probe,
 reset, init, ODR, FIFO and interrupt behaviour automatically, then walks the
 operator through the orientation, rotation and magnetometer-spin checks that
 confirm the axis conventions. Unlike imud-mon it talks to the sensor over
 I2C, so it must run on the machine the sensor is attached to, with the
 daemon stopped.

Package: libimud0
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Section: libs
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: ABI-stable client library for the imud IMU daemon
 libimud receives, validates, and decodes imud's binary telemetry (attitude,
 heading, rate of turn, heave, sensor data, fusion diagnostics) over the
 daemon's local AF_UNIX stream socket or the high-rate UDP stream. The API is
 ABI-stable: data is exposed through an append-only struct behind an opaque
 handle, so applications keep working across imud upgrades without
 recompilation. This package ships the runtime library; install libimud-dev
 to build against it (imud.h, pkg-config metadata, and libimud(3)).

Package: libimud-dev
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Section: libdevel
Depends: libimud0 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: ABI-stable client library for the imud IMU daemon (development)
 Header (imud.h), unversioned shared-library symlink, pkg-config metadata,
 and the libimud(3) manual for building applications against libimud, the
 ABI-stable client library for imud's binary telemetry stream.

Package: imud-signalk
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, imud
Description: Signal K bridge for the imud IMU daemon
 imud-signalk connects to imud's local binary stream socket and emits Signal K
 delta messages (JSON) over UDP — attitude, magnetic and true heading,
 magnetic variation, rate of turn, and heave, on standard Signal K paths in
 SI units. Runs as its own hardened systemd service and reconnects to imud
 automatically.

Package: imud-mqtt
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, imud
Description: MQTT bridge for the imud IMU daemon (with Home Assistant discovery)
 imud-mqtt connects to imud's local binary stream socket and publishes scalar
 telemetry topics (heading, attitude, rate of turn, heave, heave rate,
 temperature) to an MQTT broker via libmosquitto, plus Home Assistant
 MQTT-discovery configs so the sensors self-register as one device. Supports
 QoS, retained values, TLS, and an availability topic backed by an MQTT
 last-will.

Package: imud-influxdb
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, imud
Description: InfluxDB bridge for the imud IMU daemon
 imud-influxdb connects to imud's local binary stream socket and writes one
 InfluxDB line-protocol point per tick — quaternion, attitude, heading, rate
 of turn, heave, and the full fusion diagnostics (gyro bias and variance,
 quiescence) — over UDP or HTTP, for time-series storage and Grafana
 dashboards. Pure C, no external dependencies.

Package: imud-mavlink
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, imud
Description: MAVLink bridge for the imud IMU daemon
 imud-mavlink connects to imud's local binary stream socket and emits MAVLink
 v1 or v2 HEARTBEAT, ATTITUDE, and ATTITUDE_QUATERNION messages over UDP
 and/or a serial port, for autopilot ecosystems (ArduPilot, PX4,
 QGroundControl).
 Pure C with a hand-rolled encoder — no MAVLink library dependency.

Package: imud-prometheus
Architecture: amd64 arm64 armel armhf i386 ppc64el riscv64
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, imud
Description: Prometheus exporter for the imud IMU daemon
 imud-prometheus connects to imud's local binary stream socket and serves the
 latest fused state — attitude, heading, rate of turn, heave, the sea-state
 statistics, and the fusion/compass-health diagnostics — as Prometheus
 text-format gauges on a local /metrics endpoint, for alerting and Grafana
 dashboards. Pure C, no external dependencies; built on the ABI-stable
 libimud client library.

Package: imud-wmm-data
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Multi-Arch: foreign
Description: World Magnetic Model coefficient data for imud
 Coefficient file (WMM.COF) for the World Magnetic Model, a joint product of
 the United States' National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency (NGA) and the
 United Kingdom's Defence Geographic Centre (DGC), distributed by NOAA/NCEI.
 imud uses it to compute magnetic declination from a position fix, giving
 true heading with no network access. Packaged separately (like tzdata) so a
 new five-year model epoch can be shipped without touching the daemon.
 Architecture-independent data.
